course: dictionary
lesson: 2780
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is the context. «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak» is about food, because bubble-and-squeak is a meal of fried cabbage and potato, so dish means a meal here.
explain: «In 1928 Alexander Fleming noticed that a mould on a dish had killed the bacteria around it» is about science, not dinner. A dish here is a shallow container used in a lab to grow tiny living things. Ask: would this make sense with food in it? If not, try another meaning.
explain: «Today giant mirrors and dishes see galaxies» uses a dish that is a round, bowl-shaped object that receives signals. The sentence is about space, so a dish for food would not fit. Always test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A dish is a shallow bowl or plate for serving or cooking food.
fact: The dishes are all the plates, bowls, cups and cutlery that need washing after a meal.
fact: A satellite dish is a round, bowl-shaped object that receives signals.
fact: To dish up or dish out means to put food onto plates or to give things out to people.
fact: A dish can also be a meal, such as a favourite dish or a national dish.
exercise: What does dish mean in «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak»? | A lab container for tiny living things | A satellite that receives signals | *A food cooked in a certain way | A washing-up job
exercise: Mum asks, «Who will do the dishes tonight?» What are the dishes? | *The plates, bowls, cups and cutlery to wash after a meal | A shallow lab container | A round signal receiver
exercise: Which phrase means to put food onto plates? | Clean the floor | Dry the grass | Wash the windows | *Dish up dinner
test: In «a mould on a dish had killed the bacteria», what is the dish? | A plate for dinner | A bowl used for washing up | *A shallow container used in a lab to grow tiny living things | A meal from a menu
test: In «giant mirrors and dishes see galaxies», what is a dish? | *A round, bowl-shaped object that receives signals | A bowl used for washing up | A meal from a menu | A plate for dinner
exam: In «the heart-shaped face of a barn owl is a dish that funnels sound into its ears», what does dish mean? | A plate for dinner | *A bowl-shaped part that collects and channels sound | A dish up of food | A cooked meal
